# Git identity

- The identity for each forge comes from the `includeIf` blocks of
  `~/.config/git/identity`. Never set a local `user.email` or `user.name` in a
  repository.
- Commits are signed with SSH by the 1Password SSH signer.
- If a signature fails, tell the user to unlock 1Password. Never turn off
  signing, for example with `--no-gpg-sign` or `commit.gpgsign=false`.
- To examine the login of a forge, run `gh auth status` or `glab auth status`.
  Never print a token.
- To change the name, an email or the signing key, edit `[tools.git]` of
  `macos.toml`, then run `mise run updateall:configs`.
